ode of season 11 has to  move fast to fit in everything set up in  earlier episodes one of the most vital  arcs is that of Mercer a loyal soldier  of the Commonwealth he appears at first  to be humorless and unflappable until we  see princess's unique charm loosen him  up a bit Mercer's loyalties are in  question throughout the season his duty  to the people is in direct conflict with  his love for his sister Max who becomes  a Public Enemy after revealing Sebastian  and Pamela's callous attitudes towards  the people they're meant to serve yet  Mercer turns around in the end and  proves that there are positives to  standing by one's convictions rather  than becoming a tool of a fascist State  he shifts loyalties and takes the troops  with him when it comes time to hold  Pamela accountable he is at the front of  the group and when she calls him a  traitor he turns the tables on her you  disappeared hundreds of citizens led the  dead to our doorstep  shot a child  the Central Drive behind season 11 is  the importance of placing faith in  people rather than institutions or  politicians and nowhere is that Arc  better embodied than through Mercer a  man who refuses to live life following  orders he knows are unjust  no character in The Walking Dead has had  it particularly easy but Aaron and Lydia  have truly gone through the ringer Aaron  lost both his husband Eric and his lover  Jesus he saw his wish for a better  future for Alexandria dashed through  Lance hornsby's Lies Season 11 has him  experiencing his own dark side only to  turn things around through his  mentorship of Lydia likewise traumatized  by her years as a pawn in Alpha's game  surrounded by death and hate Lydia is in  desperate need of support and family  when she comes to the Commonwealth and  Aaron is one of the primary people to  offer it perhaps more than anyone Aaron  has always been able to put hope and the  desire to serve his friends and family  at the Forefront and that selflessness  has played